{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":74025273,"ns":0,"title":"Blackwell-Girshick equation","extract":"The Blackwell-Girshick equation is an equation in probability theory that allows for the calculation of the variance of random sums of random variables. It is the equivalent of Wald's lemma for the expectation of composite distributions.","description":"Variance of random sum","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}